Undefined is a primitive data type in JavaScript.
It represents a variable that has been declared but has not yet been assigned a value.
Example:
let age;
console.log(age); // Output: undefined
console.log(typeof age); // Output: "undefined"

null is another primitive data type in JavaScript.
It represents the intentional absence of any object value.
Example:
let data = null;
console.log(data); // Output: null
console.log(typeof data); // Output: "object"


Symbol is a primitive data type introduced in ES6.
It represents a unique and immutable value.
Example:
let sym = Symbol('description');
console.log(sym); // Output: Symbol(description)
console.log(typeof sym); // Output: "symbol"
